\text{Area of } \triangle ABC = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height} = \frac{1}{2} \times 1 \times 1 = \frac{1}{2}
\] The height of the pyramid \(ABCH\) is equal to the side length of the cube, which is 1. Now, we can calculate the volume of pyramid \(ABCH\): \[
V = \frac{1}{3} \times \text{Base Area} \times \text{Height} = \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} \times 1 = \frac{1}{6}
